# =============================================================================
# figure_3_mle_fisher_only — macro/micro roster, FINITE-DIFFERENCE Fisher against the
# analytic Gaussian one. Dispatched by ops/slurm/dispatch_figure_3_fisher_only.sh.
# Stages 2-5 ONLY (the per-group cloud and the empirical capstone are dropped).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. The Gaussian-vs-numerical Fisher comparison exists today only in
# 433ed13 (macro NR/R/MR/IR + the superseded NMR), which the manuscript declares
# superseded and quotes nothing from (04_results.tex:7, _program/provenance.md#5).
# INR, VR, LSE and ILSE were never measured at all: the _G sweep is gaussian-only and
# never forms F_b, so its Likelihood_Numerical_Fisher_Information rows carry
# bootstrap_count and no values. This script rebuilds the whole roster in ONE lane at
# HEAD so the comparison is quotable as one measurement.
#
# WHAT WAS DROPPED AND WHY. figure_3_mle_LSE_numfim.macroir runs Stages 1-6; Stage 1
# (per-group MLE over the group_size axis 1/10/100) is what makes those jobs take days
# and it feeds only Stage 6. Neither is needed for the Fisher comparison: F_b at both
# anchors comes from Stage 3 and the paired battery of Stage 5. So group_size,
# n_bootstrap_samples and min_groups_for_bootstrap are NOT injected here and must not
# be. What is lost: Cov_emp, the empirical capstone and the Optimum_Fisher_Distortion
# family. The empirical validation is already measured on the gaussian lane.
#
# TRAP 1 — WHERE THE NON-POSITIVITY IS READ. CORRECTED 2026-08-15 against this lane's
# first outputs; the note that stood here was wrong, and wrong in the direction that
# produces a confident zero. F_b at theta_sim IS indefinite over a whole region (NR:
# Δ/τ = 1 and 0.5 at every N_ch, reaching 0.2 at N_ch 1e4), and NO emitted spectrum
# shows it. When the strict PSD decomposition of F_b fails, the congruence helpers
# short-circuit on W.empty and return a ZERO matrix, so
# Eigenvalue_Spectrum<Likelihood_Gaussian_Fisher_Distortion> reads as all zeros and
# the scalar suite NaN-fills. The lenient fallback populates the spectrum of the
# matrix being decomposed, which is not F_b.
# READ IT FROM THE MATRIX: Probit_statistics_Likelihood_Numerical_Fisher_Information
# carries F_b itself (value_row/value_col, probit=mean, statistic=value), and
# eigendecomposing it offline is what gives lambda_min. See tmp/eig_fb.py.
# IN-FILE FLAG, when the matrix is not at hand: Effective_Rank_Likelihood_Fisher_
# Covariance drops below p while Effective_Rank_Gaussian_Fisher_Covariance stays at p
# (2 against 6 for NR at N_ch 1e4, Δ/τ=1). It cannot separate "negative" from "below
# tolerance", which is why the matrix is the honest source.
# STILL NEVER Min_Eigenvalue<...>: that scalar comes from compute_distortion_scalars
# (likelihood.cpp:591-595), which keeps only eigenvalues above the retention
# tolerance, so it never returns a negative and reads as a floor near zero exactly
# where the matrix is indefinite. The code comment on Min_Eigenvalue<Optimum_Fisher_
# Distortion> (cmd/likelihood.h:1012) calls it the indefiniteness readout; it is not.
#
# TRAP 2 — PER-REPLICATE INDEFINITENESS OVERSTATES IT. lambda_min is concave, so
# E[lambda_min(F_i)] <= lambda_min(E[F_i]). Measured 2026-06-10 (dirac, nsim 1024):
# negatives pervasive per replicate, but the genuine bias was ONLY NR at coarse
# sampling (lambda_min prop. -Num_ch), R at interval_in_tau=1 and MR in pockets; IR
# clean everywhere, NMR noise-only. This pipeline already does the right thing:
# compute_F_b averages F over recordings BEFORE the congruence, so what is emitted is
# the mean matrix. Never report "X% of replicates were indefinite".
#
# SEED. Injected (sim_seed), NOT the 0 sentinel: calc_seed treats 0 as "draw from
# random_device" (legacy/mcmc.h:37-45) and the resolved value is consumed locally and
# never written anywhere, so a seed=0 ensemble cannot be regenerated. That is the hole
# 433ed13 has. One seed per cell also pairs the ensemble across algorithms, which is
# what makes the cross-member comparison a comparison.
#
# COST. calc_numerical_fisher_information is 2*n_params extra likelihood passes per
# recording, run at BOTH anchors: with six free parameters, 24 passes per recording on
# top of the two dlikelihood passes, per interval. The only fit left is the single
# joint MLE of Stage 2.
#
# FILE CONTRACT — this file must NOT define the injected names itself (they must stay
# commented/undefined): axis_Nchanels, Num_ch, axis_noise, current_noise,
# n_simulations, filepath, sim_seed, algorithm_axis, algo_recursive_approximation,
# algo_averaging_approximation, algo_taylor_approximation, algo_family_approximation,
# algo_variance_form, axis_interval, exp_n_step_/exp_n_samp_, gn_max_iter,
# axis_h_fim, h_rel_value.
#
# TWO ANCHORS, two complementary questions (see theory: misspecification frame):
#   theta_sim  = the simulation truth (par_tr). The indefiniteness question lives here.
#   theta_pool = the JOINT MLE over ALL replicates (the pseudo-true value the estimator
#            centres on; a single stationary point, NOT the mean theta_bar of per-group
#            fits — those differ when the likelihood is non-quadratic). The operative
#            anchor: F_b here is the one every distortion is built on.
#
# Stages (numbering kept from figure_3_mle.macroir so the two are diffable):
#   2) JOINT MLE (group_size = n_simulations) -> theta_pool;
#   3) numerical Fisher at theta_sim AND theta_pool;
#   4) score / dlikelihood at theta_sim AND theta_pool (-> J + Gaussian Fisher G at each);
#   5) PAIRED diagnostic battery at theta_sim AND theta_pool: numerical-F-anchored and
#      Gaussian-anchored columns side by side in ONE file, which is the measurement.
# =============================================================================

model = load_model("scheme_CO")

# Dispatcher injects filepath (the run-name prefix); jobs write nch/algo-distinct files.
filepath_run = filepath

# figure_2 canonical scheme_CO values; Current_Noise and Num_ch_mean are injected.
# Six free parameters — the configuration every macro number in the paper is quoted in.
# The least-squares members run the LSE sibling of this file, which fixes two of them.
parameter = create_parameters(
   model = model,
   parameters_info = [
      {"on","Log10",10},
      {"off","Log10",100},
      {"unitary_current","Log10",1},
      {"Current_Noise","Log10",current_noise},
      {"Current_Baseline","Log10",1},
      {"Num_ch_mean","Log10", Num_ch}])

# Experiment step/sample sizes are indexed over axis_interval (injected). Three
# segments: pre @ 0 µM, agonist @ 10 µM, post @ 0 µM.
experiment = create_experiment(
   experiment_structure = [
      {exp_n_step_1, exp_n_samp_1, 0.0},
      {exp_n_step_2, exp_n_samp_2, 10.0},
      {exp_n_step_3, exp_n_samp_3, 0.0}],
   frequency_of_sampling = 50e3,
   initial_agonist = 0.0,
   initial_time = 0.0)

observations = set_observations(values_set = [0,0,0,0])

par_tr = get_standard_parameter_transformed_values(parameter)

simulation_axis = axis(name = "simulation_algorithm", labels = ["uniformization"])

simulations = simulate(
   model = model, parameter_transformed = par_tr, n_simulations = n_simulations,
   experiment = experiment, observations = observations,
   simulation_algorithm = indexed_string_by(axis = simulation_axis, values = ["uniformization"]),
   number_of_substeps = indexed_size_by(axis = simulation_axis, values = [1000]),
   seed = sim_seed)

recordings = get_recordings_from_simulations(simulations = simulations)

# Algorithm selected by the dispatcher (one per job) via algorithm_axis + the
# indexed algo_* flags — mirrors figure_2. Result is Indexed; the MLE/score
# commands broadcast over it (single algorithm here). variance_form_approximation is
# INJECTED here, where the older scripts hard-wire it to 0: it is what macro_VR needs
# (residual interval variance on MR's mean and gain), and VR is the control that
# splits the MR->IR gap into a variance step and a gain step. Every other member is
# dispatched with 0, so the injection changes nothing for them.
algorithm = build_likelihood_function_with_family(
   model = model,
   adaptive_approximation = false,
   recursive_approximation = algo_recursive_approximation,
   averaging_approximation = algo_averaging_approximation,
   variance_approximation = true,
   taylor_variance_correction = algo_taylor_approximation,
   family_approximation = algo_family_approximation,
   variance_form_approximation = algo_variance_form,
   taylor_qdt_approximation = false)

# GN inner-loop options. max_iter is injected (the dominant cost lever); the rest
# are numerical-method constants (Newton decrement is the primary convergence).
gn_opts = build_gauss_newton_options(
   lambda_kickoff = 10.0, lambda_factor = 3.0, lambda_max = 1e10,
   max_iter = gn_max_iter, grad_rtol = 1e-6, dvalue_tol = 1e-10, verbose = false)

# ---- Stage 2: JOINT MLE (group_size=n_simulations) -> theta_pool --------------
# The only fit in this script. One group, so no bootstrap over groups (n=0) and the
# min_groups guard is inert (2).
pool = calc_MLE_per_group_of_replicates(
   likelihood_algorithm = algorithm,
   theta_warmstart = par_tr,
   theta_reference = par_tr,
   experiment = experiment,
   recordings = recordings,
   group_size = n_simulations,
   n_bootstrap_samples = get_number(n = 0),
   min_groups_for_bootstrap = get_number(n = 2),
   probit_cis = [0.025, 0.16, 0.5, 0.84, 0.975],
   probit_sample_heights = [0.5],
   ranking_variables = ["Maximum_logL"],
   seed = 0,
   gauss_newton_options = gn_opts)

pool_csv = write_csv(analysis = pool, path = concat(filepath_run, "_pool"))

theta_pool = get_parameters_mean(cloud = pool)

# ---- Stage 3: numerical Fisher at theta_sim AND theta_pool -------------------
fim_sim = calc_numerical_fisher_information(
   likelihood_algorithm = algorithm, parameters = par_tr, experiment = experiment,
   data_series = simulations, h_rel = h_rel_value, decimate = 1)

fim_pool = calc_numerical_fisher_information(
   likelihood_algorithm = algorithm, parameters = theta_pool, experiment = experiment,
   data_series = simulations, h_rel = h_rel_value, decimate = 1)

# ---- Stage 4: score / dlikelihood at theta_sim AND theta_pool -----------------
# dlik_pool feeds the Gaussian bread G_bar + J (score covariance); dlik_sim is the
# Optimum-G numerator (Gaussian Fisher at the truth). Both are load-bearing here.
dlik_sim = calc_dlikelihood_predictions(
   likelihood_algorithm = algorithm, parameters = par_tr, experiment = experiment,
   data_series = simulations)

dlik_pool = calc_dlikelihood_predictions(
   likelihood_algorithm = algorithm, parameters = theta_pool, experiment = experiment,
   data_series = simulations)

# ---- Stage 5: PAIRED diagnostic battery at theta_sim AND theta_pool ------------
# The _paired command takes the numerical Fisher, so it emits the F-anchored family
# and the Gaussian-anchored one (gidm/gfc/gdcc/gdib) in the SAME file. Comparing the
# two inside one battery is the measurement this run exists for. It also emits
# Likelihood_Sample_Distortion (F-anchored) next to Gaussian_Sample_Distortion, which
# is what the micro arm of this run is for.
battery_sim = likelihood_derivative_basic_diagnostics_paired(
   dlikelihood_predictions = dlik_sim,
   numerical_fisher_information = fim_sim,
   n_boostrap_samples = 100,
   probits = [0.025, 0.16, 0.5, 0.84, 0.975], seed = 0, max_lag = 10,
   samples_dir = "")

battery_sim_csv = write_csv(analysis = battery_sim, path = concat(filepath_run, "_battery_sim"))

battery_pool = likelihood_derivative_basic_diagnostics_paired(
   dlikelihood_predictions = dlik_pool,
   numerical_fisher_information = fim_pool,
   n_boostrap_samples = 100,
   probits = [0.025, 0.16, 0.5, 0.84, 0.975], seed = 0, max_lag = 10,
   samples_dir = "")

battery_pool_csv = write_csv(analysis = battery_pool, path = concat(filepath_run, "_battery_pool"))
